<title>USA: Clinton okays disaster aid for Washington State.</title>
<headline>Clinton okays disaster aid for Washington State.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton on Monday declared Pend Oreille county in Washington state a major disaster area because of flooding caused by snowmelt, making residents eligible for federal assistance.</p>
<p>The area was stricken by flooding that began on April 10 and continued until June 30.</p>
<p>Clinton's action makes flood victims eligible for housing assistance and low-cost loans to cover ininsured losses as well as other disaster relief.</p>
</text>
